# Monitor local build and static linking

## Prefix layout

`<workspace_root>` is the directory that holds `.venv/` and `HPCPerfStats/` (the scripts' `REPO_ROOT`, i.e. `monitor/../..`). Do not hard-code a host path.

- Prefer dependency install prefix: `<workspace_root>/.build/prefix` (the `ensure_dotbuild_prefix_static.sh` default). `build_static_bundle.sh` defaults to `<workspace_root>/.build/prefix-static` with sources in `<workspace_root>/.build/src-static`; override with `PREFIX` / `SRCDIR`.
- Keep downloaded sources under `<workspace_root>/.build/src`.
- Example: on TACC (`hpcperfstats_monitor_dev`) the prefix is `/home1/01623/sharrell/hpcperfstats_monitor_dev/.build/prefix`; on hpcperfstats-dev it is `/data/HPCPerfStats/.build/prefix`.

## Third-party stack (monitor)

- **RAPL energy** (Intel/AMD `intel_rapl` / `amd64_rapl`): `src/x86_rapl.c` reads the perf `power` PMU with **`rapl_powercap.c`** `energy_uj` as per-domain fallback; no library. Do **not** use `power_read` / MSR. Do **not** reintroduce **libvariorum** or `variorum_get_energy_json` without an explicit product decision.
- **PMU / CPU counters (x86)**: direct perf through `x86_core_perf.c` (core) and `x86_uncore_perf.c` (IMC / HBM / DF) on `perf_util.c`; no library to build or link (**`monitor-x86-direct-perf.mdc`**). Since 3.1 Phases 2+3 the monitor links **no PMU library** on any arch: do not reintroduce a PMU library prefix build, configure probe or link. The backend is `--with-cpu-counter-backend={auto|x86|arm}` (`auto`: `x86` on x86, `arm` elsewhere); the CPU vendor (Intel or AMD) is read at runtime, with no compile-time vendor flag.
- **RabbitMQ / libev**: unchanged for APIs. Static **rabbitmq-c** must install as **`$PREFIX/lib/librabbitmq.a`** (`CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` in `build_static_bundle.sh` / cross). Autoconf probes `amqp_new_connection` with **`-lrt -pthread`** first (pkg-config `Libs.private`) and **`AS_UNSET`** of the search cache before a plain retry. Embedded static **libev / rabbitmq-c** must be built with **`-fPIC`** so RPM `%build` PIE / hardened-cc1 probes and final links succeed (Horizon aarch64: non-PIC `.a` → `R_AARCH64_*` / “Unable to find librabbitmq”). `prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh` and `build_static_bundle.sh` (`SKIP_DEPS=1`) must verify **`libev.a`** and **`librabbitmq.a`** before configure / `make dist`.
- **DCGM / NVML / GPUPerfAPI / Grace counters**: DCGM and NVML are `dlopen`ed at runtime (vendored headers; nothing to link). Non-x86 CPU is the **`arm` backend (`/proc/stat` util, cpufreq clock) + direct perf core and SCF counters** (no library; see **`monitor-arm-direct-perf.mdc`**). Do not reintroduce PAPI or another PMU library.

Pinned versions for scripted builds: see `HPCPerfStats/monitor/scripts/build_static_bundle.sh` (`STATIC_PIN_*`). The bundle pins only **libev** 4.33 and **rabbitmq-c** 0.18.1 static archives into `PREFIX`, plus **libbpf** for the eBPF metric profiler (no PMU library since 3.1 Phases 2+3; no hwloc/jansson build for Variorum). **rabbitmq-c** tarballs are fetched from **`alanxz/rabbitmq-c`** (default `STATIC_PIN_RABBITMQ_C_URL_FMT`); override with **`RABBITMQ_C_URL_FMT`** for mirrors.

## Static compile (`--enable-all-static`)

- Default in `configure.ac` is **`--enable-all-static`** (see `configure --help`).
- Do not append **`-lm`** into the static link group; **`Makefile.am`** keeps **`-lm`** with the usual dynamic libc stack.
- Workspace helper: `HPCPerfStats/monitor/scripts/ensure_dotbuild_prefix_static.sh` (runs `build_static_bundle.sh --deps-only` with `PREFIX=<repo>/.build/prefix`).
- Full deps + monitor build: `HPCPerfStats/monitor/scripts/build_static_bundle.sh` (or `SKIP_DEPS=1` when `PREFIX` already has the `.a` files).

## Environment for configure / make

Export when using the local prefix:

- `CPPFLAGS="-I<workspace_root>/.build/prefix/include"`
- `LDFLAGS="-L<workspace_root>/.build/prefix/lib -L<workspace_root>/.build/prefix/lib64"` (add `-Wl,-rpath,...` if you need runtime resolution for non-static parts).
- `PKG_CONFIG_PATH="<workspace_root>/.build/prefix/lib/pkgconfig:<workspace_root>/.build/prefix/lib64/pkgconfig"`

Typical minimal configure for bring-up:

- `../configure --disable-infiniband --disable-mic --disable-gpu --disable-amd-gpu --disable-opa --disable-lustre --with-systemduserunitdir=no`

CPU backend:

- x86: `--with-cpu-counter-backend=x86` (`auto` on x86_64; direct perf core, uncore and RAPL).
- aarch64: `--with-cpu-counter-backend=arm` (`auto` on aarch64).

## TACC hosts

On Stampede3 / other TACC systems (`*.tacc.utexas.edu`), load build tools via **Lmod** before the static bundle (e.g. `module load cmake` for rabbitmq-c). See **tacc-lmod-build-environment** — agent shells often need `/opt/apps/modulefiles` on `MODULEPATH` first.

## Verification

- **Canonical**: run **`scripts/build_static_bundle.sh`**, then **`make check`** in **`monitor/.build-static`**. Full policy: **monitor-static-build-verification** (always applied in this workspace).
- For **static** links, `ldd` on `hpcperfstatsd` should **not** show `libev.so` or `librabbitmq.so` from the prefix; third-party deps should be linked from `.a` inside the static group. System **libc** / **libm** / **libpthread** typically remain dynamic unless doing a full static link.

